  "question": {
    "text": "A light ray emerging from the point source placed at $\\mathrm{P}(1,3)$ is reflected at a point $\\mathrm{Q}$ in the axis of $x$. If the reflected ray passes through the point $R$ $(6,7)$, then the abscissa of $Q$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "74T0A",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6Vf1v",
      "text": "\n3\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DbARy",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hgDkO",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{5}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let abcissa of $\\mathrm{Q}=x$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/XmfDe-DYPxetuVX5pmLzY3XrhSt69t7u1RUyLw9xo1E.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\begin{aligned} \\therefore \\quad & Q=(x, 0) \\\\ & \\tan \\theta=\\frac{0-7}{x-6}, \\tan \\left(180^{\\circ}-\\theta\\right)=\\frac{0-3}{x-1}\\end{aligned}$\nNow, $\\tan \\left(180^{\\circ}-\\theta\\right)=-\\tan \\theta$\n$$\n\\therefore \\quad \\frac{-3}{x-1}=\\frac{-7}{x-6} \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{5}{2}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
